  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44116322",
      "title": "Handling HTTP Errors",
      "lectureOrder": 228,
      "videoOrder": 217,
      "sourceHash": "dfa7d359c71b9dd8d788a419253c9afdf4bbd1fc569681e4642c8f6ddbbd2a6e",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.75,
          "end": 3.96,
          "en": "Now of course things can also go wrong",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.96,
          "end": 6.21,
          "en": "when sending a request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.21,
          "end": 9.9,
          "en": "For example, there might be no internet connection,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.9,
          "end": 11.91,
          "en": "it temporarily went away.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.91,
          "end": 13.893,
          "en": "That's one possibility.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.94,
          "end": 18.42,
          "en": "But there also might be something wrong with our backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.42,
          "end": 21.213,
          "en": "and an error might occur on that backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.2,
          "end": 24.06,
          "en": "And to simulate that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.06,
          "end": 28.26,
          "en": "I will actually return a different response here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.26,
          "end": 30.27,
          "en": "after this delay.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.27,
          "end": 32.46,
          "en": "Temporarily, I'll get rid of it later,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.46,
          "end": 35.4,
          "en": "but for now I wanna return a response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.4,
          "end": 39.45,
          "en": "that sets a status code of 500.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.45,
          "end": 42.99,
          "en": "And that's how you can do this in Node and Express.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.99,
          "end": 46.77,
          "en": "This creates a response with a status code of 500,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.77,
          "end": 49.65,
          "en": "and I'll call the json method on that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.65,
          "end": 52.77,
          "en": "to then really finalize that response,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 52.77,
          "end": 53.673,
          "en": "so to say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.99,
          "end": 58.95,
          "en": "So now this route will no longer return the places,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 58.95,
          "end": 61.893,
          "en": "but instead this error response,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63,
          "end": 65.1,
          "en": "and of course nobody would do that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.1,
          "end": 69.063,
          "en": "but for simulating the error use case, this is perfect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 70.23,
          "end": 72.72,
          "en": "You now just have to go back to that terminal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 72.72,
          "end": 76.56,
          "en": "where you started your backend development server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 76.56,
          "end": 79.05,
          "en": "and quit it by pressing Ctrl C",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 79.05,
          "end": 80.16,
          "en": "and restart it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 80.16,
          "end": 83.193,
          "en": "so that those code changes are picked up.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 85.28999999999999,
          "end": 86.73,
          "en": "With that, if you now reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 86.73,
          "end": 89.1,
          "en": "you'll see that we're fetching those places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 89.1,
          "end": 92.07300000000001,
          "en": "and then they never arrive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 93.21000000000001,
          "end": 96.81,
          "en": "And we see an error here in the developer tools",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 96.81,
          "end": 99.723,
          "en": "that we got some HTTP related error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 101.19,
          "end": 105.42,
          "en": "Well, how can we now handle that in our component?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 105.42,
          "end": 109.62,
          "en": "Well, for example, again, by adding an extra signal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 109.62,
          "end": 112.38,
          "en": "an error signal for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 112.38,
          "end": 115.14,
          "en": "though the name of course is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 115.14,
          "end": 117.27000000000001,
          "en": "And that could store a string value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 117.27000000000001,
          "end": 119.1,
          "en": "So the error message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 119.1,
          "end": 122.07,
          "en": "And initially that could be an empty string since initially",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 122.07,
          "end": 123.873,
          "en": "we don't have any error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 125.43,
          "end": 128.22,
          "en": "But then I wanna set this signal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 128.22,
          "end": 132,
          "en": "to the error message if an error occurs here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 132,
          "end": 134.7,
          "en": "And for that, we can add that third",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 134.7,
          "end": 138.54,
          "en": "and last function to our observer object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 138.54,
          "end": 140.91,
          "en": "the error function, which will be triggered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 140.91,
          "end": 144.9,
          "en": "whenever some error is thrown somewhere",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 144.9,
          "end": 147.09,
          "en": "in that observable chain.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 147.09,
          "end": 150.12,
          "en": "And Angular will produce an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 150.12,
          "end": 152.76,
          "en": "if something goes wrong technically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 152.76,
          "end": 156,
          "en": "so if we have no internet connection for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 156,
          "end": 159.03,
          "en": "or if we get an error response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 159.03,
          "end": 163.38,
          "en": "In both cases, Angular will produce an error value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 163.38,
          "end": 166.23,
          "en": "and this function will get triggered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 166.23,
          "end": 169.82999999999998,
          "en": "and it will receive that error information then.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 169.82999999999998,
          "end": 174.06,
          "en": "So in here, we could then use our error signal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 174.06,
          "end": 177.78,
          "en": "and set it to that error we're getting here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 177.78,
          "end": 181.53,
          "en": "It's worth noting that TypeScript doesn't know what type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 181.53,
          "end": 183.36,
          "en": "of value we'll get here though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 183.36,
          "end": 186.42,
          "en": "Nonetheless, we can try setting it like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 186.42,
          "end": 188.19,
          "en": "and then we can of course go back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 188.19,
          "end": 192.72,
          "en": "to the available places template and add another check here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 192.72,
          "end": 196.05,
          "en": "and also update this first check",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 196.05,
          "end": 199.02,
          "en": "because now here we can check if we're fetching",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 199.02,
          "end": 202.98,
          "en": "and error is falsey.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 202.98,
          "end": 207.98,
          "en": "So this error signal produces a falsey value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 208.2,
          "end": 211.2,
          "en": "In that case, I wanna show this loading text,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 211.2,
          "end": 213.36,
          "en": "but otherwise if we're not fetching",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 213.36,
          "end": 216.51,
          "en": "or we have an error, I don't want to show that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 216.51,
          "end": 219.15,
          "en": "And instead we can add another if check here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 219.15,
          "end": 223.59,
          "en": "and check if error produces a truthy value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 223.59,
          "end": 226.44299999999998,
          "en": "so if the error signal has a non empty string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 227.4,
          "end": 231.48,
          "en": "and in that case I want to output a paragraph with the class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 231.48,
          "end": 234.81,
          "en": "fallback-text on it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 234.81,
          "end": 237.603,
          "en": "that will output that error message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 238.59,
          "end": 240.69,
          "en": "So we can use string interpolation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 240.69,
          "end": 244.113,
          "en": "to output the value stored in the error signal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 247.47,
          "end": 251.46,
          "en": "And if you save that all and you reload, you'll see that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 251.46,
          "end": 255.513,
          "en": "after a while you get this object Object thing here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 256.92,
          "end": 257.97,
          "en": "And we're getting this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 257.97,
          "end": 260.88,
          "en": "because this error we're getting here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 260.88,
          "end": 262.86,
          "en": "in this error function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 262.86,
          "end": 265.26,
          "en": "this argument here is actually not",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 265.26,
          "end": 266.46,
          "en": "an error message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 266.46,
          "end": 268.44,
          "en": "Instead it's an error object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 268.44,
          "end": 272.85,
          "en": "which however should contain a message property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 272.85,
          "end": 275.373,
          "en": "So we can try accessing it like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 277.71,
          "end": 279.45,
          "en": "And with that, if we reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 279.45,
          "end": 281.67,
          "en": "we can again try fetching those places and",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 281.67,
          "end": 284.73,
          "en": "after a while we get some message,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 284.73,
          "end": 289.23,
          "en": "however, not really a user-friendly message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 289.23,
          "end": 293.52,
          "en": "So what we might wanna do instead is maybe log",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 293.52,
          "end": 296.1,
          "en": "that error for ourselves,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 296.1,
          "end": 299.463,
          "en": "but show a more user-friendly message here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 301.02,
          "end": 302.19,
          "en": "And we could of course do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 302.19,
          "end": 305.403,
          "en": "by simply console logging the error here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 306.24,
          "end": 309.15,
          "en": "Or alternatively, we could try sending it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 309.15,
          "end": 312.18,
          "en": "to some analytics server if we had any.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 312.18,
          "end": 313.6,
          "en": "Here, I'll just log it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 314.49,
          "end": 317.377,
          "en": "and then maybe output some hardcoded message like",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 317.377,
          "end": 320.52,
          "en": "\"Something went wrong",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 320.52,
          "end": 324.57,
          "en": "fetching the available places.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 324.57,
          "end": 326.907,
          "en": "Please try again later.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 328.2,
          "end": 331.2,
          "en": "That is something we could do here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 331.2,
          "end": 333.96,
          "en": "And if we save that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 333.96,
          "end": 337.47,
          "en": "and we reload, we should see that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 337.47,
          "end": 339.24,
          "en": "more user-friendly message here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 339.24,
          "end": 341.97,
          "en": "And we still log that error object here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 341.97,
          "end": 344.913,
          "en": "which now contains more details about the error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 346.02,
          "end": 349.8,
          "en": "But again, we could also use an operator here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 349.8,
          "end": 351.33,
          "en": "not because we have to,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 351.33,
          "end": 355.263,
          "en": "but because we can, to keep these observer functions leaner.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 356.58,
          "end": 358.68,
          "en": "And therefore we can add a second argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 358.68,
          "end": 361.08,
          "en": "to this pipe method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 361.08,
          "end": 363.93,
          "en": "And after adding this map operator,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 363.93,
          "end": 367.923,
          "en": "we can add the catchError operator,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 369.18,
          "end": 373.383,
          "en": "which is another operator that's imported from RxJS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 375.96,
          "end": 377.43,
          "en": "And catchError does",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 377.43,
          "end": 378.99,
          "en": "what its name implies.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 378.99,
          "end": 380.7,
          "en": "It in the end is responsible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 380.7,
          "end": 382.11,
          "en": "for handling errors,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 382.11,
          "end": 384.903,
          "en": "and for potentially transforming errors.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 385.98,
          "end": 388.71,
          "en": "For that, it takes a function just like map.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 388.71,
          "end": 393.71,
          "en": "And that function takes an argument, a parameter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 393.75,
          "end": 398.4,
          "en": "which in the end is that error that we got.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 398.4,
          "end": 400.74,
          "en": "It actually also takes a second argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 400.74,
          "end": 403.89,
          "en": "which is that observable that emitted that error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 403.89,
          "end": 407.31,
          "en": "So this observable that's created by get.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 407.31,
          "end": 409.353,
          "en": "But here I only care about the error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 410.31,
          "end": 412.83,
          "en": "And then catchError actually needs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 412.83,
          "end": 415.923,
          "en": "to return a new observable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 416.82,
          "end": 420.54,
          "en": "So unlike map, it should now not return some data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 420.54,
          "end": 423.18,
          "en": "to which this error has been converted,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 423.18,
          "end": 426.693,
          "en": "but instead it must return a new observable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 427.98,
          "end": 430.56,
          "en": "And I'll generate a new observable here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 430.56,
          "end": 432.2,
          "en": "by calling throwError,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 434.04,
          "end": 435.93,
